hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27620","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, he said: Haddathana Abu Usamah, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Zur'ah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from a freedman of Ma'mar al-Taymi, from Asma' bint Umays, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: With what did you seek cure? She said: With shubrum. He said: Hot and intense. Then I sought cure with senna. He said: If anything cured death, senna would, or: senna is a cure from death."
"27621","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Musa al-Juhani, he said: I entered upon Fatimah bint Ali, and my companion Abu Sahl said to her: How old are you? She said: Eighty-six years. He said: Did you hear anything from your father? She said: Asma' bint Umays narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"27622","Haddathana Waki': Haddathana Abd al-Aziz, he said: Haddathana Hilal, our freedman, from Abu Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from his mother Asma' bint Umays, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me words to say at distress: Allah is my Lord, I associate nothing with Him."
"27623","Haddathana Yazid, he said: Anba'ana Muhammad ibn Talhah, he said: Haddathana al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Asma' bint Umays, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me on the third day after the killing of Ja'far and said: Do not mourn beyond this day of yours."
"27624","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Asma' bint Umays, that she gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at al-Bayda', and Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Command her to bathe and then enter ihram."
"27625","Haddathana Ya'qub, he said: My father narrated to me from al-Walid ibn Kathir, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muslim al-Tawil, keeper of the mushafs, narrated to me that Kilab ibn Talid, brother of Banu Sa'd ibn Layth, while he was sitting with Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, the messenger of Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im ibn Adi came to him saying: Your cousin sends salam to you and says: Inform me how is the hadith that you narrated to me from Asma' bint Umays. So Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab said: Inform him that Asma' bint Umays informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: None endures the hardship and severity of Madinah except that I will be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"27626","Haddathana Ya'qub, he said: My father narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Isa al-Jazzar, from Umm Ja'far bint Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Talib, from her grandmother Asma' bint Umays, she said: When Ja'far and his companions were struck, I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I had tanned forty skins, kneaded my dough, washed my sons, oiled them and cleaned them. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bring me the sons of Ja'far. She said: So I brought them to him, and he smelled them and his eyes shed tears. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, what makes you weep? Has anything reached you about Ja'far and his companions? He said: Yes, they were struck this day. She said: So I stood screaming, and the women gathered to me, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to his family and said: Do not neglect the family of Ja'far by making food for them, for they are preoccupied with the affair of their companion."
